  "file": "rule-of-the-octave.musa",
  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The Rule of the Octave: one chord for each degree of the bass scale." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// OMT `035-galant-schemas-the-rule-of-the-octave-and-harmonizing-the-scale-" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// with-sequences.md` states the Rule as a recipe — parallel 6/3 chords, then" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// 5/3 on the tonic, then 5/3 on the dominant, then a seventh before each of" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// those — and `std::tonal::schemas` is that recipe written as functions. This" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// piece asks the library for the chords and decides, itself, how they sound." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The same eight chords are played twice, under two policies that share no" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// decision: close position from a low bass in quarter notes, and drop-2 from a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// higher bass in halves. Nothing in the library chose either. That is the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// point of the file: a harmonic skeleton is not music until somebody voices it," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// and the library never does." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"The Rule of the Octave\"" },
